+CJK adjacency changes flanking when punctuation would otherwise prevent a
+delimiter run from opening or closing emphasis:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+これは**「重要なこと」**です。
+.
+<p>これは<strong>「重要なこと」</strong>です。</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+これは**私のやりたかったこと。**だからするの。
+.
+<p>これは<strong>私のやりたかったこと。</strong>だからするの。</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+The same flanking definition applies to single delimiters:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語*「引用」*語
+.
+<p>語<em>「引用」</em>語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+Chinese punctuation and Korean text are CJK characters under the definition
+above:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+**。**话
+.
+<p><strong>。</strong>话</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+**안녕(hello)**하세요.
+.
+<p><strong>안녕(hello)</strong>하세요.</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+Only the characters next to each delimiter run determine the CJK alternative.
+The content itself may use ASCII punctuation or occur in mixed text:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語**(ABC)**語
+.
+<p>語<strong>(ABC)</strong>語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+a**「x」**b
+.
+<p>a<strong>「x」</strong>b</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+a**（x）**b
+.
+<p>a<strong>（x）</strong>b</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+a**㊙x**b
+.
+<p>a<strong>㊙x</strong>b</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+An excluded emoji may still be emphasized when CJK characters outside the
+delimiter runs provide the adjacency:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語**😀**文
+.
+<p>語<strong>😀</strong>文</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+Supplementary-plane CJK characters have the same effect:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+𠮷**(U+20BB7)**語
+.
+<p>𠮷<strong>(U+20BB7)</strong>語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+The existing delimiter matching and precedence rules remain in effect:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語***「引用」***語
+.
+<p>語<em><strong>「引用」</strong></em>語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語**「*引用*」**語
+.
+<p>語<strong>「<em>引用</em>」</strong>語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語**[項目](https://example.com)。**文
+.
+<p>語<strong><a href="https://example.com">項目</a>。</strong>文</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語**`code`。**文
+.
+<p>語<strong><code>code</code>。</strong>文</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+Ambiguous-width punctuation does not trigger the CJK alternative:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+a**“x”**b
+.
+<p>a**“x”**b</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+The additional restrictions on underscore delimiters remain unchanged:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語__「強調」__語
+.
+<p>語__「強調」__語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+CJK adjacency does not override either whitespace condition:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語** 強調**語
+.
+<p>語** 強調**語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+語**強調 **語
+.
+<p>語**強調 **語</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+Default emoji presentation does not count as CJK by itself:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+a**😀。**b
+.
+<p>a**😀。**b</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+The definition examines immediate characters, not variation sequences or
+characters from other scripts:
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+禰󠄀**(ね)**豆子
+.
+<p>禰󠄀**(ね)**豆子</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
+```````````````````````````````` example
+ไทย**(ข้อความ)**ไทย
+.
+<p>ไทย**(ข้อความ)**ไทย</p>
+````````````````````````````````
+
